To manage the messages with CAPL it is important know if the message is transmitted or received.
If a DBC is loaded in the CANalyzer or CANoe configuration it is possible call the desired message.
The l’ID, DLC, signals and other properties are imported automatically.
Sintax:
message <id or message name> <variable name>
message STATUS_BCM
msgSTS_BCM;
// it is possible use even the ID
message 0x100 msgSTS_BCM;

Every property should be defined, in the following example DLC is defined:
message 0x100 msgSTS_BCM = {DLC = 8};
//DLC assigned during the declaration
msgSTS_BCM.DLC = 8;
//DLC assigned after
How to use the Messages

In the following it is created a function «TX_STATUS_BCM» in which are manipulated 2 signals and then the message is
transmitted with the «output»:
STATUS_BCM msgSTS_BCM
TX_STATUS_BCM
{
msgSTS_BCM.VehicleSpeed.phys = @sysvar::BCM::Set_VehicleSpeed;
msgSTATUS_BCM.RechargeSts = 1;
output(msgSTS_BCM);
}
